[00:22.83][04:32.75]Welcome to the fiction
[00:26.84][04:36.79]We hide here every evening
[00:30.99][04:40.94]With plenty of exuberance
[00:35.17][04:45.13]And voices for the voiceless
[00:40.08]But if I look out on the floor
[00:42.35]Is there room for any more?
[00:44.62]I'm a buzzkill and a bore
[00:46.42]I'm not the person this is for
[00:48.71]But I'm tired of civil war
[00:50.54]My spirit is screaming out for more
[00:52.81]It's all just too much to ignore
[00:55.83]That I could be something more
[01:04.33](We could be something more)
[01:15.22][02:22.58][03:44.26]The sprawl of the ballroom with the lights down low
[01:19.39][02:26.74][03:48.26]I know you see my eyes aglow
[01:23.65][02:30.99]My hand is extended to offer you a dance
[01:27.88]By chance, would you welcome my romance?
[01:30.98]And we both know, it's fantasy
[01:36.86](But the feeling is real and it's real for you and me)
[01:40.53][02:47.89]The sprawl of the ballroom
[01:42.48](With the lights down low)
[01:46.44]I'm a grease spill and a bad time
[01:50.48]So I look around me, see the fault lines
[01:54.75]Every soul here has a problem
[01:58.90]But when they're together, they are flawless
[02:04.32]But there's no pretending nothing's wrong
[02:06.42]They'll figure it out that I'm a fraud
[02:08.42]But I still try to play along
[02:10.93]'Cause I just want to belong
[02:16.72](Do I belong?)
[02:35.21]Advance, my darling take a chance
[02:38.36]And we're no kings, you and I
[02:44.20](But being together, we're royalty tonight)
[02:50.12](Hold me close)
[02:57.94]I'm so tired of the fiction
[03:00.66](Who are we)
[03:02.13]I get so caught up in the friction
[03:04.77](You and me)
[03:06.28]But it's okay to let it go
[03:08.71](We can be so free)
[03:10.33]And find a comfort in the show
[03:14.16](A thing nobody knows)
